{"id": "meta_modelers_guide.composites.fig06-mechanistic", "name": "F\u2081F\u2092 ATP Synthase \u2014 Mechanistic Rotary Motor (load sweep \u2192 stall \u2192 reversal)", "description": "Fig 6 upgraded to a real reduced rotary-motor model (AtpSynthaseRotor). The membrane holds a proton-motive force \u0394p = 150 mV; a MechanicalLoad ramps the external shaft torque linearly past the stall point. Torque, speed, proton/ATP flux, the power split and efficiency are all DERIVED from \u0394p, the ATP free energy \u0394G_ATP, and the load \u2014 not imposed. Over the 20-tick run the rotor turns forward (synthesising ATP), slows as the load rises, STALLS when \u03c4_ext = \u03c4_drive\u2212\u03c4_chem (\u2248 tick 10), then REVERSES (\u03c9<0 \u2192 ATP hydrolysis pumping protons). The power budget P_in = P_ATP + P_ext + P_heat closes exactly on every step. This is the mechanistic variant of fig06-runnable (kept as the algebraic didactic baseline).", "parameters": {}, "state": {"rotor": {"_type": "process", "address": "local:AtpSynthaseRotor", "interval": 1.0, "config": {"n_c": 10.0, "atp_per_rev": 3.0, "drag": 1e-23, "dg0_kjmol": 30.5, "temperature": 298.15, "buffer_pools": true, "min_conc": 1e-06}, "inputs": {"pmf": ["membrane", "pmf"], "load_torque": ["load", "torque"], "atp": ["pools", "atp"], "adp": ["pools", "adp"], "pi": ["pools", "pi"]}, "outputs": {"omega": ["signals", "omega"], "angle": ["signals", "angle"], "proton_flux": ["signals", "proton_flux"], "proton_current": ["signals", "proton_current"], "atp_flux": ["signals", "atp_flux"], "drive_torque": ["signals", "drive_torque"], "chem_torque": ["signals", "chem_torque"], "net_torque": ["signals", "net_torque"], "dg_atp": ["signals", "dg_atp"], "power_in": ["signals", "power_in"], "power_atp": ["signals", "power_atp"], "power_ext": ["signals", "power_ext"], "power_heat": ["signals", "power_heat"], "efficiency": ["signals", "efficiency"], "atp": ["pools", "atp"], "adp": ["pools", "adp"], "pi": ["pools", "pi"]}, "int